      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The serpentine belt drives essential components like the alternator, water pump, and power steering system to keep your engine functioning correctly. If this belt goes bad due to wear, glaze, or a loose tensioner, it can slip against the pulleys, especially under the sudden load of accelerating. This slipping creates the loud squealing noise you are hearing during acceleration. You should soon visit a mechanic to check the belt and tensioner to prevent further damage to your engine.",
