      "content": "While the belt may appear intact, it could still be glazed or hardened on the inside, causing slip. Additionally, the power steering pump or water pump might have excessive bearing drag, forcing the belt to work harder than normal and slip under acceleration. Finally, the automatic tensioner arm might be worn or broken, failing to maintain proper belt tightness. These issues all require checking specifically after listening to diagnose the exact source of the noise.",
